en', 'native_title_verified', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 0, 'American Journal of Audiology', NULL, '29', '1', '6', '17', NULL, 'American Speech Language Hearing Association', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '10.1044/2019_aja-19-0010', NULL, NULL, NULL, '1059-0889', 'https://doi.org/10.1044/2019_aja-19-0010', NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, 'clinical', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'COMPLETE', 'VERIFIED', 'RESOLVED', NULL, NULL, 0, NULL, NULL, 'Expected a replication of REF-00578 in hearing-aid users. Confirmed, and it adds something my prior did not contain: it states that peer-reviewed data supporting the 0.3 s requirement were NOT previously available for hearing-aid wearers, i.e. the ANSI standard''s own footnote rested on conference proceedings until this paper. That makes the standard''s provenance weaker than I had assumed, not stronger.', 'see search_executions exec 10-15 for this batch (verbatim, logged before screening)', NULL, ' || ADMITTED 2026-08-22 by PROMOTION from source_locators, ref_id REUSED. Companion to REF-00578 in hearing-aid users. YEAR: 2020 per the retrieved Crossref payload (vol 29, iss 1, pp 6-17); the DOI slug reads 2019 because that is the assignment year, and an earlier note in exec 14 wrongly inferred 2019 from the slug before the payload corrected it.', '2026-08-22 05:28', 'session_2026-08-22-research-batch-02-room-acoustic-performance', '2026-08-22', 'session_2026-08-22-research-batch-02-room-acoustic-performance', 'crossref', NULL, 1, NULL, '6-17', 3, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'high_control', 'pending', 'pending', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'tool', NULL);
